[[File:Gryphon icon.png|left]]
[[File:Gryphon Safespot West Cave .png|thumb|Gryphon safe spot on the Great Conch island.  It is the cave on the west side. Avoids all attacks.]]
'''Gryphons''' are [[Slayer monster]]s requiring 51 [[Slayer]] to kill. They inhabit the [[Great Conch]] and require completion of the [[Troubled Tortugans]] quest and 45 [[Sailing]] to access. [[Wings Spread]] must be unlocked at a slayer master for 80 points to be given as a task by [[Nieve]] or [[Duradel]]. You can also get this task from [[Chaeldar]], [[Vannaka]] or [[Mortimer]] without unlocking them with points as long as the quest is completed. They commonly attack [[Tortugan]]s.

Gryphons attack with [[melee]] and have a special attack allowing them to knock back players with too low of an '''equipped''' [[weight]] with a threshold of 30kg. If the player's equipped weight meets this threshold, a gryphon using the special attack will be stunned instead; additionally, the player may click the Gryphon within 2 ticks of it being stunned to knock it back one tile and perform one additional attack free of attack delay. Unlike the boss and superior variants, the player will not be punished for missing this counter-attack. Despite its use in the prerequisite quest, a [[tortugan shield]] does '''not''' have to be equipped while fighting normal gryphons. It is, however, required for both the superior and boss variants and is generally recommended due to its considerable weight. Gryphons have an elemental weakness to [[air spells]], but melee is typically a stronger option, especially considering that melee armour is typically heavier.

With the Slayer reward ''Bigger and Badder'' unlocked for 50 [[Slayer reward point]]s, there is a chance for their [[Superior slayer monster|superior]] version, the [[dire gryphon]], to spawn. It has the same mechanics as regular gryphons, except the players will take guaranteed damage after every hit if a [[tortugan shield]] is not equipped and the weight threshold for the knockback is increased to 40kg. It is therefore recommended to adjust your gear accordingly in case a superior spawns.

A boss variant, the [[shellbane gryphon]], can be fought while on task.

During the quest [[Troubled Tortugans]], [[Elder Raley]] requests that an aggressive gryphon be tracked down and killed after it attacks the village and retreats to the forest. It can be tracked to a cave north of [[The Summer Shore]], where it is fought.

==Locations==
Gryphons can be found in two dungeons: a task-only [[Gryphon Caves|eastern cave]] and a western cave in which they may be fought off-task. Both caves have a mix of [[Single-way combat|single-way]] areas and [[multicombat area]]s that are cannonable. The multicombat areas are limited to a single southern room in each cave.
